func=jag::PacketHandlers::SetMapFlag	func_addr=0x00186de0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt op 0x24 (size 10, fixed). Reads 10 bytes: b0\estartX-delta, b1\estartY-delta(0x80-x), b2..b5\e32-bit packed colour, b6\eendY-delta(0x80-x), b7\eheight/angle(-0x80), b8\eflag(int8,-1 sentinel), b9\eendX-delta(0x80-x, read only when b1!\e0xff). Computes absolute fine coords as (delta + SceneManager.base[+0x608/+0x60c]) * 0x200. Calls helper FUN_00227a70 which does jag::InterfaceManager::CreateOrFindUpdateEntry(client->interfaceMgr\e__DT_RELA[0xcf7], type\e0xE, key\e0) and writes TWO coordinate slots (start +0x40, end +0x60) + colour. Singleton (key 0) interface update entry of type 0xE holding start/end tile coords + colour. Sibling CS2 opcode FUN_0015abf0 builds the SAME type-0xE entry from entity GraphNode world translations and uses it to highlight entities -> entry \e on-screen/world marker overlay (hint/route/highlight). Cursor: variable per branch but bounded to the 10-byte fixed payload. CONFIDENCE: opcode+size CONFIRMED; category\eInterfaces well-supported (InterfaceManager + CreateOrFindUpdateEntry; all other callers of that fn are IF_* handlers). Exact canonical IF_/marker name UNRESOLVED -> HYPOTHESIS, name left UNKNOWN.
