func=jag::PacketHandlers::PointlightColour	func_addr=0x001dec60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt handler op\e0xD7, fixed size\e8 (u32BE value [byteswapped on LE host], u16 duration (low byte raw+0x80... transformed), u16LE effectTypeId). Cursor advances exactly 8 bytes (verified).\nSUBSYSTEM: same as op0xB6 - SceneManager(Client+0x19558) -> current World -> FUN_006195e0 collects all world effect-emitter instances with instance+0x80 \e\e effectTypeId.\nSEMANTICS: duration converted to cycles via *(uint*)(Client+0x4F8), start \e *(int*)(Client+0x500) (CLIENT_CYCLE). Writes the instance's U32 TWEEN block: value\e\e0xFFFFFFFF -> target +0x54 \e default +0x4C (revert to default); else +0x54 \e value. +0x58 \e current (copied from +0x50), +0x5C \e startCycle + durationCycles (end), +0x60 \e startCycle, +0x64 \e startCycle. u32 is read big-endian and reverts to a stored default - RGBA colour-like.\nHYPOTHESIS (not confirmed): tween a packed u32 (likely RGBA colour/tint) of all effect instances of a type over a duration, 0xFFFFFFFF \e reset to default. Canonical RS name unknown - family postdates the librs2client.so reference.\nDISCREPANCY: engine ServerProt.kt calls this NPC_SET_COLOR_TINT / Category.NPC_INFO - wrong subsystem (instances are world effect emitters, not NPCs).\nConfidence: wiring+behavior CERTAIN; semantic name UNKNOWN.
