func=jag::PacketHandlers::NpcInfo	func_addr=0x001d7b60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=126	text=NPC_INFO (ServerProt op52, varShort) wire format — PHASE 1 (update known NPCs). NpcManager \e Client+0x194b8 (\enpcList_00/R12). gBit(8) here \e count of currently-known NPCs to process. The known-slot array is at NpcManager+0xa0a0 (int[]), count at +0xb0a0; tick counter +0xc0e4; removal vector +0xb0a8; ext-info queue vector +0xc0f0; new-NPC coord bit width at +0xc0e8 (set by REBUILD_NORMAL body[6], default 7). Per known NPC: see 0x1d7cf2 (1-bit hasUpdate + 2-bit movement type).
func=jag::PacketHandlers::NpcInfo	func_addr=0x001d7b60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=402	text=PHASE 1 per-known-NPC encoding. gBit(1)\ehasUpdate; if 0 -> NPC unchanged (stays). If 1: gBit(2)\emovementType: 0\eext-info-only (no move, always enqueued for Phase 3); 1\eWALK (gBit(3) dir, then gBit(1) hasExtInfo); 2\eRUN/multi-step (gBit(1) sub: 0->1x gBit(3) dir, 1->2x gBit(3) dirs; then gBit(1) hasExtInfo); 3\eREMOVE from local list (no further bits, NPC dropped). Direction 0..7 \e 8-compass (DecodeMoveCode @0x143ab0). REMOVE value \e movementType 3.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::NpcInfo	func_addr=0x001d7b60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=826	text=PHASE 2 add-new-NPC loop. Runs while >\e16 payload bits remain. Add-record field order (binary-verified by gBit call sites): gBit(16) slotIndex (0xFFFF\eterminator, ends phase) @1d7e9a; gBit(1) flag @1d7f35 (teleport/jump bool, 4th arg to position vcall+0x170); gBit(coordW) deltaY @1d7f49; gBit(coordW) deltaX @1d7f60 (coordW \e NpcManager+0xc0e8, default 7; both sign-extended by half-range); gBit(16) typeId @1d7f7c (-> SetType vcall+0x220); gBit(1) hasExtInfo @1d7f93 (enqueues for Phase 3); gBit(2) level/plane @1d7fa5; gBit(3) spawnFacing @1d7fb8. NOTE: deltaY precedes deltaX; level is read AFTER type+hasExtInfo, NOT between the coords.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::NpcInfo	func_addr=0x001d7b60	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=986	text=NpcInfo new-NPC add: ESI \e NpcManager+0xc0e8 (the NPC-info local-coord BIT WIDTH set by REBUILD op81 byte+6 / op83 byte+0). Passed to jag::Packet::Bit::gBit (0x13e970) here for local-x, and again @1d7f4e for local-z. @1d8040 the same N is used as 1<<(N-1) to sign-fold the unsigned coord. Confirms Camera/scene size is unrelated to this; +0xc0e8 is the per-rebuild NPC coordinate resolution.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::NpcInfo	func_addr=0x001d7b60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=1331	text=COORD FRAME ANSWER (op52 NPC add): NPC position \e LOCAL PLAYER live grid pos + delta, NOT scene base / rebuild origin. R13\e[NpcManager+0xc0d8]\eClient; [Client+0x19b30] -> FUN_00198b40 resolves the local player PathingEntity by index (live). If player has no pending move (entity+0x268 seg count @+0x30 \e\e0): GetPositionGrid(player) -> {plane,Xtile,Ytile}; else uses player last-queued waypoint tile. Then Xfine\e(deltaX+playerXtile)*512+256, Yfine\e(deltaY+playerYtile)*512+256 (512\efine/tile @cb6ae4, 256\ehalf-tile center @cb6b2c). Delta is a TILE difference in the SAME frame the player sits in, so scene base cancels: server delta \e npc.absTile - localPlayer.LIVE_absTile is correct at ANY player position. Hypothesis (scene-base/last-rebuild relative) is REFUTED.
