func=jag::game::HeightMap::SampleRegionFineHeight	func_addr=0x0041fa50	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=Inner fine-height sampler called by jag::game::HeightMap::GetFineHeight. Picks the region's height\ncontainer: primary at regionHeightData+0x90, fallback at +0xeb88. A container is READY (usable) only\nwhen byte[+0x11] \e\e byte[+0x12] (CMP/JZ at 0x41fa6e); otherwise it falls through to the fallback,\nthen fails. byte[+0x159] !\e 0 \e> not loaded (writes height 0). Plane vertex grid: vec at +0x160..+0x168\n(0x10-byte elems), plane grid \e *(begin + 8 + plane*0x10); for plane 0 with usePlane0Bridge it uses\n+0x1e8 instead. Bilinear-interpolates the per-vertex int32 heights: col\e(fineX>>9)+1, row\e(fineY>>9)+1,\ncolumns 0x18 apart, blend over (fineX&0x1ff)/(fineY&0x1ff) with >>9. Writes the result straight to\n*heightOut with NO scale factor (heights are already in fine-Z units, 512/tile). When addTileLinkOffset\n!\e 0 it adds FUN_003ffcf0 (tile-link / plane-bridge height addend). Replicated read-only in engine\nHeightMap.kt. usePlane0Bridge/addTileLinkOffset names are HYPOTHESIS (exact caller semantics unverified).
