func=jag::signal_handling::FatalSignalHandler	func_addr=0x00acfab0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=jag::signal_handling FATAL SIGNAL HANDLER (sa_handler installed by _INIT_0 for SIGHUP(1), SIGILL(4), SIGBUS(7), SIGFPE(8), SIGSEGV(0xb), SIGSYS(0x1f)).\n\nCONFIDENCE: CONFIRMED. Evidence:\n- Registered as DAT_015beb00 \e FUN_00acfab0 in _INIT_0 @ 0x000c0438 with sa_flags 0x48000000, applied via 6 sigaction() calls for exactly those 6 signals.\n- Maps signum -> human string ("Invalid pointer access","Bus error (bad memory access)","Floating point exception","Illegal instruction","Hangup detected","Bad system call") + strsignal(); formats "Signal %s (%s)".\n- Captures up to 100 backtrace frames via FUN_00cb4920(FUN_00a87e50,...) (\e jag::callstack::capture_stack_back_trace in ref binary).\n- Dispatches the crash report: per-thread SEH handler at fs:[-0x1f19] if present (vtable+0xd0), else the GLOBAL reporter object DAT_015beb98 -> calls FUN_0047d5b0/FUN_0047d4f0 -> jag::game::ClientError::ReportError (FUN_006ef050) which POSTs to nxtclienterror.ws.\n- AFTER reporting: calls FUN_00ab1020() (resets all 6 signals to SIG_DFL) then raise(signum) to re-trigger default action (core dump / propagate to launcher rs3linux).\n\nThis is the "phones home on crash" entry. The actual network send is in ReportError (FUN_006ef050).\n\nSUPPRESSION HOOK OPTIONS:\n(A) Hook FatalSignalHandler -> immediately call FUN_00ab1020() then raise(signum) and return (skip report). Reproduces the default-action behavior with NO telemetry. LOW RISK.\n(B) Preferred: hook ReportError (FUN_006ef050) instead so script/fatal paths are covered too; this handler will then run, "report" nothing, reset signals, and re-raise normally.\nRISK of fully no-op'ing this handler without re-raising: process would hang/loop on the faulting instruction (signal re-delivered) -> ALWAYS keep the reset+raise tail.
