func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal — ServerProt op81 (0x51), varShort. ProtEntry @0x013a1360; bound in ServerProt::BindHandlers.\n\nGPI PREFIX: if ConnectionManager(Client+0x19440)+0x49 set (first scene rebuild after (re)login), first calls PlayerList::HandleAbsolutePlayerPositions (FUN_00b254a0) consuming the bit-packed GPI init block (gBit(30) local + 2046x gBit(20) low-res), then byte-aligns. ~5119B for a full list; 5119+18 \e 5137 \e observed login packet. Subsequent rebuilds: 18-byte header only.\n\n18-BYTE SCENE HEADER (read AFTER optional GPI block), real offsets verified from disasm:\n  b0      pad (stored to [RSP], unused beyond playerZoneY low byte)\n  b1..b2  playerZoneY  (LE u16: b1\elow, b2\ehigh)            [reads @1daab9/1daabf, combined @1dabbb]\n  b3      MAGIC 0x85   (equality check ONLY @1dab40; reject->PacketError. NOT a size.)\n  b4..b5  playerZoneX  (BE u16, ROL8 @1daaf7)\n  b6      NPC-INFO COORD BIT WIDTH (readUByteAdd: (raw-0x80)&0xff) -> NpcManager(Client+0x194b8)+0xc0e8.\n          NOT 'playerLocal', NOT a camera angle. Consumed by NpcInfo via gBit() (see 1dabc2 / 1d7f3a).\n  b7      pad\n  b8..b9  worldId/instance id (BE u16, ROL8) -> resolves the bound World region\n  b10..b13 g4 packed coord1 -> BuildArea::DecodePackedCoord (local_60)\n  b14..b17 g4 packed coord2 -> BuildArea::DecodePackedCoord (local_54)\n\nSCENE SIZE IS NOT SENT. Scene base corner \e (playerZone - centerOffset)*8, centerOffset \e Camera[0x610]>>4.\nCamera[0x610] is FIXED 0x100 (256) from the Camera ctor (FUN_000851ae @0x8582a) and is written nowhere else\nin .text \e> centerOffset \e 16 (constant) for overworld AND instances. SetSceneBase (FUN_00143fa0) sets\n+0x604/+0x608/+0x60c per rebuild but PRESERVES +0x610. The legacy 2012 mapSize byte (104/120/136/168/72)\nhas NO equivalent here. (Supersedes the earlier centerOffset\e6 / 104-tile HYPOTHESIS, which the binary disproves.)
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=plate	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=Setting prototype: undefined * REBUILD_NORMAL_SIMPLE(long * thisPtr, PacketCore * packetPtr)
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=143	text=REBUILD_NORMAL body[8..9] BE u16 (ROL8) -> [RSP+0x1e]\elocal_6a \e worldAreaType \e jag::game::WorldAreaType CACHE CONFIG ID (NOT worldId/instance). Observed 474(0x01da) surface, 674(0x02a2). Consumed at 0x1daee9. Only zero-extended; used as raw id/key.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=150	text=REBUILD_NORMAL byte+6 transform: ESI \e (rawByte - 0x80) & 0xff  \e\e  readUByteAdd (g1_add). Server encodes with writeByteAdd: wireByte \e value + 128. Decoded result stored at 1dabc2.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=183	text=srcPackedCoord1 \e REBUILD_NORMAL body[10..13] (g4 BE). BuildArea::DecodePackedCoord -> {plane\e(v>>28)&3, x\e(v>>14)&0x3FFF, y\ev&0x3FFF} at local_60/5c/58. This is the SW (min) corner of the new World's map-square grid (passed as x>>6,y>>6 \e map squares to CreateWorldFromWorldArea). Surface login value: 0x01a00940 \e (x1664,y2368) \e mapsq(26,37). Constant per world area; server-supplied (not in client binary).
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=203	text=srcPackedCoord2 \e REBUILD_NORMAL body[14..17] (g4 BE). BuildArea::DecodePackedCoord -> {plane,x,y} at local_54/50/4c. This is the NE (max) corner of the new World's map-square grid. Surface login value: 0x048e23b8 \e (x4664,y9144) \e mapsq(72,142). Together with srcPackedCoord1 it defines the World's inclusive map-square rectangle: (NE.x>>6 - SW.x>>6 +1) x (NE.y>>6 - SW.y>>6 +1) \e 47x106 cells for the surface. Server-supplied \e world area bounding rectangle.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=208	text=REBUILD_NORMAL byte+3 \e protocol MAGIC 0x85 (-0x7b). R14B \e b3 (loaded @1daac9). EQUALITY CHECK ONLY: if !\e0x85 -> return PacketError (DAT_015d35c0). R14 is NEVER used as size/index/shift afterward (it is overwritten at 1dabc9 with Camera[0x610]). 0x85 is a pure version/magic sentinel, NOT a size field.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=338	text=b6 decoded value -> NpcManager(Client+0x194b8)+0xc0e8 \e NPC-INFO LOCAL-COORD BIT WIDTH (Ghidra renders the dest as __DT_RELA[0x428]+*(Client+__DT_RELA[0xcfb]); the REAL store is `mov [NpcManager+0xc0e8], EBX`). Read by NpcInfo as gBit(N) for new-NPC x/z. This is the only server-supplied 'size-like' value in op81 and it is a coordinate resolution, not the build-area tile size.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=338	text=byte+6 (decoded, readUByteAdd) -> NpcManager(Client+0x194b8)+0xc0e8. This field is the NPC-INFO LOCAL-COORDINATE BIT WIDTH, NOT a camera angle/size. Read by jag::PacketHandlers::NpcInfo: @1d7f3a and @1d7f4e it is passed to jag::Packet::Bit::gBit (0x13e970) to read a new NPC's local x then z; @1d8040 it computes 1<<(N-1) for sign-folding. op83 REBUILD_REGION writes the SAME field @1df209 from ITS byte+0 (transform readUByteSubtract). So this is the only "size-like" value the server sends here, and it is an NPC coord resolution, not the legacy map-size enum.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=345	text=SCENE-BASE compute (CORRECTED, binary-verified). Ghidra's `*(int*)(lVar17+0x610)` is Camera(Client+0x19420)+0x610. centerOffset \e Camera[0x610] >> 4. Camera[0x610] \e FIXED 0x100 (256) set only by the Camera ctor (FUN_000851ae @0x8582a); NO packet/runtime writer exists \e> centerOffset \e 16 (constant). baseX \e (playerZoneX-16)*8 ; baseY \e (playerZoneY-16)*8. Passed to SetSceneBase(FUN_00143fa0) which writes +0x604/+0x608/+0x60c but preserves +0x610. Server does NOT control scene size. (Earlier centerOffset\e6 / base610\e0x60 note was a hypothesis; the ctor value 0x100 disproves it.)
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=345	text=Camera(Client+0x19420)+0x610 \e build-area SIZE field. Value is FIXED 0x100 (256), set ONCE in the Camera ctor at FUN_000851ae+0x8582a and NEVER written by any packet handler or runtime code (exhaustive c7/89/c6/88/66:89/0f11/0f29 store scan over .text found no other Camera writer). centerOffset(zones) \e value>>4 \e 16. This is NOT server-controlled.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=eol	insn_offset_from_entry=359	text=centerOffset \e Camera[0x610] >> 4 \e 256>>4 \e 16 zones. Scene SW-corner tile \e (playerZone - 16)*8 for BOTH X and Y (player centred, 16 zones / 128 tiles each side). Fixed client-side; identical for op81 REBUILD_NORMAL and op83 REBUILD_REGION (both READ this, neither writes it).
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=455	text=op81 REBUILD_NORMAL: reads renderer->field_0x10108 (current bound World region, RBX\erenderer slot ptr) and compares to RSI (the NEWLY-resolved region). RSI \e (SceneManager(Client+0x18cb8).field_0x3c\e\e4 && worldArray[DAT_015df084]!\e0) ? resolveWorld(worldId\ebody+8 u16)->[8] : DAT_015d4d60(default)->[8]. If equal -> skip rebuild (0x1dae48); else teardown+rebuild via SceneManager build (constructs a new renderer bound to RSI). If RSI (resolved world region) is null, the new renderer's field_0x10108 is null -> later world-login crash in FUN_00647fc0. HYPOTHESIS: for a plain overworld the default-world path is taken; the crash means the client had no valid active World when this ran (enter-game/world-create prerequisite unmet) and/or worldAreaTypeId/build-rectangle resolved to a null world.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=887	text=CALL jag::game::SceneManager::CreateWorldFromWorldArea (true entry 0xc56160; decompiler mislabels it 'FUN_00c55e80').\nArgs: RDI\eSceneMgr(Client+0x19558), RSI\e&worldAreaSharedPtr(local), EDX\ecoord1.x>>6, ECX\ecoord1.y>>6, R8D\ecoord2.x>>6, R9D\ecoord2.y>>6 \e the World map-square grid SW & NE corners.\ncoord1\esrcPackedCoord1 (body[10..13]) -> SW corner; coord2\esrcPackedCoord2 (body[14..17]) -> NE corner. For overworld surface (WorldAreaType 474): SW\emapsq(26,37), NE\emapsq(72,142), constant & player-independent. World is then built covering that inclusive map-square rectangle.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::RebuildNormal	func_addr=0x001daa70	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=1145	text=worldAreaType CONSUMER: virtual [vtable+0x40](list, worldAreaType, 0) \e\e ConfigTypeListLoadAll<jag::game::WorldAreaType>::List(id, statusOut\enull) -> shared_ptr<WorldAreaType> (indexes list+0x58 by id*0x10). list \e registry(Client+0x18cb8)[+0x80][ordinal DAT_015df084\e0x53]+0x38. Returned shared_ptr<WorldAreaType> is (a) region [ret+8] compared vs renderer+0x10108 to skip/rebuild, (b) passed to SceneManager::CreateWorldFromWorldArea -> World::World. Value \e RAW WorldAreaType config id.
func=jag::ClientProt::SendClientCheat	func_addr=0x002807d0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=jag::ClientProt::SendClientCheat -> ClientProt::CLIENT_CHEAT (op0, varByte). Sends a typed ::console command.\nTrims whitespace from the command string, then: p1 count(\eutf8CharCount+4, 3 if empty), p1 flagA(param_3),\np1 flagB(param_4), then the command as a null-terminated CP1252 string (pStringUTF8ToCP1252).
func=jag::minimenuactions::ThreeDView::DoOpLoc	func_addr=0x0015c5f0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=jag::minimenuactions::ThreeDView::DoOpLoc (948-5, scenery). ProtEntry selects opcode. (was SendOpLocTLong)\nOPLOC1\eop125, OPLOC2\eop111, OPLOC3\eop109, OPLOC4\eop41, OPLOC5\eop126, OPLOC6\eop2(examine), OPLOCT\eop18.\nPlain (else) wire \e size 9:\n [0]   ctrl-run flag writeByteAdd (bit0)\n [1-4] locId  (MiniMenuEntry+0x48\ePARAM_1) writeInt (4-byte BE, raw)\n [5-6] worldX (MiniMenuEntry+0x4c\ePARAM_2) writeShortAddLittle (LE, low+128)\n [7-8] worldY (MiniMenuEntry+0x50\ePARAM_3) writeShortAddLittle (LE, low+128)
