func=jag::PacketHandlers::NpcHeadiconSpecific	func_addr=0x001d7860	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt handler op\e0xa0, size\e9 (fixed). CATEGORY: NPCInfo/Animations (CERTAIN it is NPC-targeted). OPCODE NAME: UNKNOWN.\nPAYLOAD (9 bytes): [u16 npcIndex big-endian][u8 b2][s8 b3][u8 b4][u8 b5][u8 b6][u8 b7][s8 slotSel].\nFLOW: node \e NPCList::GetNPCNode(Client+0x194b8 \e NPC_MANAGER, npcIndex); npc \e *(node+8); if null -> return. Lazily allocates a 0x98-byte ext-anim sub-struct at npc+0x1108 (two parallel int[8] arrays at sub+0x0 and sub+0x48, both init to 0xffffffff). slot \e (0x80 - slotSel) & 0xff (0..7). arr0[slot] \e b4<<16 | b5<<24 | b6 | b7<<8 (packed two u16: looks like id + delay). arr1[slot] \e (s16)(b2<<8 | ((b3-0x80)&0xff)) (signed height/offset). Then jag::PathingEntity::ApplyExtendedAnimations(npc).\nENGINE CALL CHAIN: NPC_MANAGER(0x194b8) -> GetNPCNode -> PathingEntity::ApplyExtendedAnimations (both already-named symbols).\nEVIDENCE: (1) NPC_MANAGER offset matches Offsets.kt OClient.NPC_MANAGER\e0x194b8; (2) GetNPCNode + ApplyExtendedAnimations named; (3) 8-slot id/height/delay triple \e spotanim/animation slot data.\nHYPOTHESIS: per-NPC spotanim/extended-animation slot update (NPC_SPOTANIM/NPC_ANIM family). Canonical name + exact slot semantics unverified -> UNKNOWN.\nSELF-CHECK: cursor advances 2+2+4+1 \e 9 bytes. OK.\nENGINE NOTE: npc+0x1108 ext-anim sub-struct (0x98 bytes) is NOT in Offsets.kt -> candidate new offset.
