func=jag::game::ClientError::ReportError	func_addr=0x006ef050	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=jag::game::ClientError::ReportError(ClientError* this, char const* message, Callstack const* callstack, uint flags)\n\n*** PRIMARY EXTERNAL CRASH/ERROR TELEMETRY PATH ("phones home") ***\n\nCONFIDENCE: CONFIRMED. Evidence:\n- Builds URL "%s/nxtclienterror.ws?clientToken\e%s&timeStamp\e%llu&c\e%d&cs\e%d&nxt\e%s&u\e%s&cid\e%d&devbuild\e%d" (string @ 0x00fd5658). nxtclienterror.ws \e Jagex client-error reporting endpoint.\n- Reference binary librs2client.so has jag::game::ClientError::ReportError(JagException const&, char const*, bool) with matching param shape (this, message, Callstack*, flag).\n- Packs error message string + backtrace (each frame relocated via dladdr against DAT_015bec68 \e base anchor FUN_000c04a0) into a jag::Packet (FUN_00c45fe0/FUN_00191580), builds "data\e" POST body, and SENDS synchronously via libcurl (FUN_008a0c90 \e curl multi/transfer), then tears down the request (FUN_0089cc50). Upload is IN-PROCESS, not deferred to launcher.\n\nflags bitmask (param_4): &4 \e> take the network-report branch (build URL + curl POST); &1 \e> append callstack frames from param_3; &2 \e> extra. Signal handler passes 7 (\e4|2|1). Script errors pass (param_6 & 5).\n\nCalled from: signal/crash handler FUN_00acfab0 (via FUN_0047d5b0/FUN_0047d4f0); fatal/terminate handler FUN_00ad3ee0; jag::ScriptRunner::ReportScriptError @ 0x00315407; FUN_0047d440; FUN_0048d080; FUN_008b5c50.\n\nSUPPRESSION HOOK POINT: hook here and return immediately to neutralize ALL client-error/crash telemetry (signal crashes, fatal errors, script errors) in one place. Safe: callers ignore the return value. Alternative finer-grained masking: scrub message/callstack before the curl send.
