func=jag::PlayerEntityBaseAppearanceDecoder::DecodeBaseAppearanceAsPlayer	func_addr=0x00141b40	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=jag::PlayerEntityBaseAppearanceDecoder::DecodeBaseAppearanceAsPlayer (\e\e ref @0x0051ed20; structurally identical, version-drift constants differ). 'this' (param_1) \e base decoder obj (\e outer decoder model+0x20). Buffer copy @ this+0xa8 (param_1[0x2a]), working pos @ this+0xb0 (param_1[0x2c]), region_start @ this+0xd8, region length written to this+0xdc (param_1[0x2f]) \e pos-region_start (caller advances outer pos by this).\nDecodes the EQUIPMENT/BODY region of the player appearance. WIRE ORDER (VERIFIED 948-5):\n A) PER WEAR SLOT (count N \e cache PlayerModelWearSlot list, this+0x88->+0x18cb8 cfgprovider +0x260, *list\ecount, list+0x10\etype[]):\n      for slot i with type[i]!\e1 (type\e\e1 slots emit NO byte):\n        b0 \e g1. if b0\e\e0 -> slot empty (bodyPart\e-1, obj\e-1), 1 byte total.\n        else b1 \e g1; v \e (b0<<8)|b1 (big-endian u16), 2 bytes total.\n          if i\e\e0 && v\e\e0xffff -> OBJ-MORPH: objId \e gSmart2or4s + 1 byte (param_1[2]); skip remaining slots.\n          else if v < this[1](\e0x800) -> BODY PART model id \e v - this[0](\e0x100).   [VERIFIED threshold 0x800 via disasm @0x141d98; ref used 0x4000 - DRIFT]\n          else -> WORN ITEM id \e v - 0x800.  (item loads ObjType for recolor base)\n B) if NOT obj-morph (slot0 objId\e\e-1): recolorMask \e g2 (FUN_00121a30). Then for each type\e\e0 slot whose bit is set in recolorMask (bit index increments per type\e\e0 slot): per-slot ObjTypeCustomisation override:\n      cflags \e g1; if&1: 2x gSmart2or4s [+2 more if base recolor!\e-1]; if&2: 2x gSmart2or4s [+2 more]; if&4: g2 packed(4x4bit) then up to 4x g2; if&8: g1 packed(2x4bit) then up to 2x g2.\n C) ARRAY1: exactly 10 bytes (FUN_00c46090 size\e10). each g1, validated vs cfg(+0x240)+0x60 sublist size else forced 0; byte ALWAYS consumed.\n D) ARRAY2: exactly 10 bytes (same, vs cfg+0x240+0xb8 sublist).\n E) BAS id \e g2 (signed, FUN_00121a00) -> this+0xc/param_1[3]. references 'bas' cache config (gameval bas: 1\ehuman_1). -1\euse cache default.\nFor a naked default human: all slots either body-part(v\eid+0x100) or 0x00; recolorMask\e0; arrays\e10x00 each; BAS\e1 or -1.
