func=jag::packethandlers::ZoneUpdates::UPDATE_ZONE_FULL_FOLLOWS	func_addr=0x000f7bb0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=UPDATE_ZONE_FULL_FOLLOWS body — ServerProt op78 (FIXED 3 bytes), reached via thunk 0x000f9510. Sets the current-zone base globals (g_baseLevel/g_baseTileX/g_baseTileY) consumed by every zone sub-content handler (ObjAdd, LocAddChange, ...).\nWire (asm-verified @0f7c0d..0f7c7d):\n  body[0] LEVEL : readUByteAdd       -> g_baseLevel \e (b0-0x80)&0xff        [enc writeByteAdd]\n  body[1] zoneY : readUByteSubtract  -> zoneYeff \e (signed)(0x80 - b1)      [enc writeByteSubtract]\n  body[2] zoneX : signed raw byte    -> zoneXeff \e (int8)b2                 [enc writeByte]\n  g_baseTileX \e Camera[0x608] + zoneXeff*8 ; g_baseTileY \e Camera[0x60c] + zoneYeff*8\nCamera[0x608]\esceneBaseX\e(playerZoneX-16)*8, Camera[0x60c]\esceneBaseY\e(playerZoneY-16)*8 (set per-rebuild by REBUILD_NORMAL/SetSceneBase FUN_00143fa0). centerOffset 16 \e Camera[0x610]>>4; Camera[0x610]\e0x100 FIXED in Camera ctor @0x0008582a (sole writer).\n\e> zoneXeff \e absZoneX - playerZoneX + 16 ; absTileX \e (playerZoneX-16+zoneXeff)*8 + xInZone (xInZone 0..7 from sub-packet packedCoord).\nASYMMETRY: X wire byte \e zoneXeff (raw); Y wire byte \e 0x80 - zoneYeff (subtract). The '10..22 centered on 16' range is the EFFECTIVE index, NOT the raw Y wire byte (which is 0x80-eff \e 106..118).
