func=jag::PacketHandlers::PointlightExtendAbove	func_addr=0x001dbd40	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt handler op\e0xB6, fixed size\e3 (u16LE effectTypeId, u8 mode). Cursor advances exactly 3 bytes (verified).\nSUBSYSTEM (confirmed from target): Client+0x19558 \e SCENE_MANAGER (engine OClient.SCENE_MANAGER); SceneManager+0x70 \e CURRENT_WORLD_INDEX, +0x58 \e WORLD_ARRAY (0x10-byte entries, entry+8 \e World*; -1 -> default entry DAT_015df2b0). FUN_006195e0 scans the World's effect-instance hash map at World+0xc01c8 (buckets +0xc01d0) and collects every instance (0x2f0 bytes, refcounted, vtable PTR_FUN_01367ea0, owns a GraphNode) whose int field instance+0x80 \e\e effectTypeId.\nSEMANTICS: mode is decoded as (0x80 - raw): 0xF -> CLEAR the bool override (instance+0x155\e0); else SET override: instance+0x154 \e (mode\e\e1), +0x155\e1. Tri-state remote bool override #3 of the instance's override block (+0x150..+0x15F).\nFAMILY: ops 0x96(+0x156/157), 0x81(+0x152/153), 0xCB(+0x150/151 + progress 0xE8), 0x99(float +0x158/15C), 0x9A(float tween +0x68..7C), 0xD7(u32 tween +0x4C..64) all target the same instances. Instances are spawned per-tile from map data (FUN_0045a160: tile*512 coords, MapSquare::GetUnderRoofLevelForZone, LinkMap::GetTileLink) and entity-attached (NPCEntity::UpdateAABB), GraphNode::SetSourceBounds in ctor FUN_00425ba0 \e> RENDERABLE world effect emitters (particle-emitter/light-like), NOT NPCs, NOT audio.\nHYPOTHESIS (not confirmed - do not rename to specific name): pause/enable-style bool override for all world effect emitters of a given type. Canonical RS name unknown; this packet family postdates the librs2client.so reference (old jag::game::World has no such registry; reference Audio/ZoneUpdates categories lack these shapes).\nDISCREPANCY: engine ServerProt.kt names this NPC_SET_DRAW_QUEUE_FLAG / Category.NPC_INFO - WRONG subsystem (objects are world effect instances, looked up via SceneManager, field layout incompatible with Entity/NPC structs).\nConfidence: wiring+behavior CERTAIN; semantic name UNKNOWN.
