func=jag::PacketHandlers::CamShake	func_addr=0x00175ae0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt op 0x6f (111), FIXED size 6. Sig: undefined*(long* thisPtr, long packet) __stdcall.\nReads 6 bytes b0..b5 (cursor +6 exactly, self-check OK), then calls virtual method *(Camera+0x248)+0x148 with this\eCamera+0x248 and args:\n  a \e (b4 - 128) & 0xff\n  b \e b5 (raw)\n  c \e (-128 - b3) & 0xff\n  d \e ((b1<<8) | ((b0-128)&0xff)) & 0xffff   // 16-bit coordinate\n  e \e b2 (raw)\nCamera \e *(Client + 0x19420)  [RELA idx 0xcf5] (engine OClient.CAMERA\e0x19420, confirmed).\nTail: increments *(Client+0x19450)+0x10 and sets +0x14\e1  [RELA idx 0xcf7] -- the camera-updated marker, BYTE-IDENTICAL to CAM_RESET and CAM_SMOOTHRESET in THIS binary.\nCATEGORY \e Camera -- CERTAIN (Camera manager + shared camera-update marker, both same-binary proof).\nSPECIFIC OPCODE \e UNKNOWN. HYPOTHESIS: positional camera packet (CAM_MOVETO or CAM_LOOKAT) -- 16-bit coord + angle/speed bytes calling a Camera sub-controller method; cannot disambiguate eye-vs-lookat sub-controller, so name not committed.\nConfidence: category CERTAIN, specific HYPOTHESIS. Ref jag::packethandlers::Camera::Camera binds ~10 lambdas (pattern-only).
