func=jag::InterfaceManager::DrawSlotChildren	func_addr=0x002b3210	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=jag::InterfaceManager::DrawSlotChildren(ifManager, slotVec, slotScreenX, slotScreenY, origScreenX, origScreenY, parentW, parentH, dt) — iterates over a parent component's child slot vector and draws each child, applying scissor/scroll clipping and special handling for slot type 0x57d. The slotVec is the InterfaceParent's component vector (parent+0x8). Layout: { InterfaceComponentSlot* begin; InterfaceComponentSlot* end; InterfaceComponentSlot* capacity; }. Each slot is 0x18 bytes: removed-flag at +0, shared_ptr value (InterfaceComponent*) at +0x10. The loop walks begin..end stepping 0x18, skipping slots whose removed byte is non-zero. Per child: 1. Read child's parentRelX (+0x50) + slotScreenX, parentRelY (+0x54) + slotScreenY \e screen-absolute position. 2. Skip if vtable +0x18 returns 0x57d (special skip-marker). 3. For non-skipped children: call vtable +0x78 (width) and +0x80 (height) checks; if visible and in scissor rect (ifManager+0x18cd0), invoke vtable +0x40 (Draw) with screen position + dt (XMM0). 4. Otherwise call vtable +0x48 (alternate draw with no position). Same +0x18cd0 scissor field, same 0x57d skip marker, same vtable slots (+0x18/+0x40/+0x48/+0x78/+0x80), InterfaceManager flag bits at +0x2fc/+0x2fe/+0x2ff, 9-parameter signature with float dt in XMM0. Reached via tail-call from DrawLayer which checks the parent's vtable+0x8 then calls with (parent - 0x10) to adjust from InterfaceParent pointer to ifManager base.
