func=jag::Packet::gScrambledByte	func_addr=0x0047f840	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=jag::Packet::gScrambledByte — signed-byte read whose transform is chosen by the cipher-selector byte at packet+0x28 (post-incremented; points at an in-binary const table, NOT the wire). The 4 modes ARE the standard jag byte transforms:\n  0 -> raw                 \e readUByte (g1)\n  1 -> wire-128            \e readUByteAdd (g1_add)\n  2 -> -wire               \e readUByteInverse (g1_neg)\n  3 -> 128-wire            \e readUByteSubtract (g1_sub)   [binary: -0x80 - (signed)wire]\nProcessExtendedInfo uses this for the APPEARANCE block length: cipher table APPEARANCE_EXTINFO_SCRAMBLE_CIPHER[0]\e3 -> appLen \e readUByteSubtract \e (128 - wireByte). Server writes appLen wire byte \e writeByteSubtract(realLen) \e (128-realLen)&0xff. VERIFIED 948-5 (live capture appLen wire\e0x3d -> 67).
