func=eastl::rbtree::next	func_addr=0x00aa5050	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=eastl::rbtree::next — standard EASTL/STL red-black tree successor iteration. Node layout (offsets in bytes): +0x00 pointer to left child, +0x08 pointer to right child (NEXT in iteration order), +0x10 pointer to parent. Node payload starts after +0x18 (varies by node type). Algorithm: if node has a right child (+0x08 !\e null), descend to its leftmost node and return it; otherwise walk up via parent (+0x10) until arriving from a left child (came-from-right keeps walking up), returning that parent (or the node itself if the root is hit). Used heavily to iterate static-location / world trees with a sentinel node.
func=jag::PacketHandlers::ShowFaceHere	func_addr=0x00173bd0	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt Camera-category handler (opcode 0x9D, fixed size 1) — exact opcode UNKNOWN.\nReads 1 byte b; writes Camera+0x620 \e (-(uint)b) & 0xFF (bool broadcast: 0 -> 0, nonzero -> 0xFF) on the camera object at Client+0x19420 (engine OClient.CAMERA \e jag::game::Camera, verified 948-5). Then marks the camera-dirty notifier at Client+0x19450: counter (+0x10)++ and flag (+0x14)\e1. Advances cursor by 1 \e payload size (self-check OK).\nCATEGORY CONFIDENCE: CERTAIN \e Camera. Writes the engine-confirmed Camera object, and the (+0x10++ / +0x14\e1) dirty-bump idiom on the adjacent notifier matches reference jag::packethandlers::Camera CAM_REMOVEROOF (lambda#9 _M_invoke @ librs2client.so, which bumps a scene/camera-dirty object the same way).\nSPECIFIC OPCODE: NOT determinable. No 1-byte bool-store-to-camera-field handler exists in the outdated reference Camera set {CAMERA_UPDATE, CAM2_ENABLE, CAM_RESET, CAM_FORCEANGLE, CAM_MOVETO, CAM_LOOKAT, CAM_SMOOTHRESET, CAM_SHAKE, CAM_REMOVEROOF, CUTSCENE} (CAM2_ENABLE calls ResetCamera; CAM_REMOVEROOF reads 4 bytes). Likely a camera/scene visibility toggle stored as a 0/0xFF mask. Left as UNKNOWN pending verification — do not rename without confirming the Camera+0x620 field meaning.
