func=jag::PacketHandlers::CreateCheckEmailReply	func_addr=0x00173f60	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=ServerProt CREATE_CHECK_EMAIL_REPLY (opcode 0xC0, fixed size 1). Account-creation "is this email available?" reply status.\nReads 1 byte b; validates b is in allowed set {2,3,20,21} via bitmask test ((1<<(b+3)) & 0x1800063, with b+3<0x19), else defaults to 3; stores the int result to LobbyManager+0x34.\nManager \e Client+0x19400 (jag::packethandlers Lobby / account-creation manager). Field +0x34 is the sibling of +0x38 (CREATE_CHECK_NAME_REPLY). Advances cursor by 1 \e payload size (self-check OK).\nCONFIDENCE: CERTAIN. Byte-identical to reference jag::packethandlers::Lobby::Lobby(jag::Client&) lambda#2 _M_invoke @ librs2client.so 0x001a4972 — same field offset +0x34, same validation mask 0x1800063, same default 3, same code shape. Reference jag::ConnectionManager::ConnectionManager binds lambda#2 to ServerProt::g_serverProt_CREATE_CHECK_EMAIL_REPLY. (Reference manager offset Client+0x7D8 vs target 0x19400 \e version drift.)
