func=jag::ClientProt::SendSceneGraphReport	func_addr=0x00229f40	kind=pre	insn_offset_from_entry=0	text=CRASH FAULT SITE (948 lobby SIGSEGV). Deepest non-machinery frame in the crash backtrace (returns into LoginProtocolHandler). Called UNCONDITIONALLY once per lobby frame from jag::ConnectionManager::LoginProtocolHandler with param_1 \e *(connState + 0x19450).\n\nHYPOTHESIS (NOT confirmed - do not rename): per-frame "RunCollectedEventList"-style flush. Beta has jag::InterfaceManager::RunCollectedEventList with the same role (drain a collected per-frame event list) but a drifted body; this 948 version walks two eastl::rbtree event queues at param_1+0x20 / param_1+0x28 and applies each via FUN_00228630, then conditionally Packet::SendClientMessage. Behavioral match is partial (version drift) -> left as FUN.\n\nWalks pending interface-component update events queued by IF_OPENTOP (kind 0xc) / IF_OPENSUB (kind 0xb) via InterfaceManager::CreateOrFindUpdateEntry. FUN_00228630 (per-event applier) calls jag::game::InterfaceList::GetStaticComponent(ifaceList+0x30, event.componentId) and dereferences *(component+8). A queued event referencing a component whose parent interface was opened with a bad packed id yields a bad/dangling component pointer -> SIGSEGV here.
